Third-party attribution notices for binary distributions of aisotropyd
======================================================================

aisotropyd statically links (CGO_ENABLED=0) Go modules licensed under the
Apache License 2.0. Apache-2.0 §4(d) requires any distributed derivative work
to include a readable copy of the attribution notices contained in a NOTICE
file shipped by those modules. This file aggregates every such NOTICE found in
the dependency tree; the Dockerfile copies it into the published image next to
the binary, together with the project's own LICENSE and NOTICE (Apache-2.0
since ADR-0080 — this project is now on the giving end of §4(d) too).

Regenerate the inventory (from the repo root, read-only):

  for d in $(go list -m -f '{{.Dir}}' all 2>/dev/null); do
    [ -f "$d/NOTICE" ] && { echo "--- $d"; cat "$d/NOTICE"; }
  done

Audited 2026-07-23: of the Apache-2.0 modules linked into aisotropyd
(badger, qdrant/go-client, wazero, OpenTelemetry, jsonschema/v6, lingua-go),
only wazero ships a NOTICE file.

